export anchor ApothecaryStyle:
    number: 86
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Apothecary
    idea: An old pharmacy counter in black and gold on cream, where each project is a numbered bottle filled to its progress and every figure sits on a framed label with a Latin-style caption.
    base: light
    palette:
        cream: #f4eedd, the page
        label: #fbf7ea, labels, the day book, the register and fields
        drawer: #e9dfc4, cabinet drawer fronts
        jet: #17140f, text, the fascia, frames, bars and the primary button
        umber: #4f4536, the shelf, the cabinet body and notes
        goldLeaf: #b08d3c, inner frames, rules, bottle scales and the focus ring, never text
        goldInk: #6b5114, Latin captions on cream
        goldOnJet: #d8b968, lettering and lines on the fascia
        tincture: #c9862b, the liquid in each bottle, never text
        verdigris: #1f5f52, On track
        sienna: #8a4b0e, At risk
        carmine: #8e1b22, Behind and overdue
    type:
        Two stacks. Didone uses Didot, Bodoni 72, Bodoni MT, Big Caslon,
        Georgia, serif for the 46px greeting, 48px drawer numbers, 30px
        brand in caps tracked 0.3em, 26px section titles in caps and 18px
        bottle names, plus 12 to 14px caps tracked 0.2em for labels, nav
        and buttons. Book uses Hoefler Text, Baskerville, Georgia, serif at
        17px with 1.55 line height, with 14 to 15px italic gold ink for the
        Latin-style captions.
    layout:
        A black fascia with a doubled gold lower edge holds the spaced
        caps brand, the italic line dispensary of projects, an underlined
        search, the gold framed New project button, a round bell and the
        user. The nav sits centred below on cream, the current item in a
        double frame. The greeting is centred in a large oval label with
        a doubled gold and black ring, captioned Salve, and under it a
        tilted carmine stamp with an hourglass says 4 tasks are overdue.
        The four numbers are drawers in an umber cabinet, each with a
        framed label holder, a Latin caption, a big number and a brass
        knob. The shelf is a row of six identical bottles whose amber
        liquid rises to each percentage, with a small label showing the
        percentage and a gold scale beside, standing on a thick umber
        shelf. Under each bottle a framed card gives the roman numeral,
        name, ex team caption, tasks, due date and status. Below, a day
        book lists numbered entries and a register shows fourteen
        horizontal measures, hatched for last week and solid black for
        this week. Below 1000px bottles go three across and the lower
        panels stack, and two across on a phone.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 48px between counter sections, 16px between bottles and 8px cabinet joints.
    density: Medium. Ordered rows of identical vessels and drawers, all centred.
    corners: Square labels and drawers. Curves only in the oval greeting, the bottle shoulders and oval swatches.
    borders: A 1px jet outline with a 3px gap and an inner gold hairline on every label. A double gold rule under the fascia.
    shadows: None. Depth comes from nested frames and the umber shelf.
    icons:
        Thin line glyphs at text size. On track is a ring with a dot, At
        risk an outlined triangle, Behind a solid square and overdue an
        hourglass, each with its caps word between two hairlines.
    focus: A 2px jet outline offset 4px, a cream gap, then a 3px gold ring. On the fascia the outline is gold on jet.
    tone: Measured and old-fashioned with Latin-style captions, such as The shelf, Day book, Register, Opera activa and Attend first.
